{% doc %}
  Smart Color Contrast Override System

  When a custom background color is set:
  - check if the global settings.page_text_color provides sufficient contrast against the background,
    - if yes, use it as the text color
    - if no, use the palette extreme (lightest or darkest) that best contrasts the background

  Effective text colors are exposed as CSS custom properties in snippets/palette-vars.liquid.

  Presets control which token categories of CSS variables are emitted:
  - 'content' (default) — base + text + border + form-disabled + accent
                          (the original content-rich behaviour used by sections/blocks)
  - 'ui'                — base + text + border + form-disabled
                          (lightweight UI surfaces: popover, drawer, badges)

  Form tokens that exist only on .color-custom-{id} (never on .text-block prose
  containers): --input-disabled-*, --checkbox-border.

  Input chrome (--color-input-*) is not emitted by this snippet — inputs use the
  global Input Fields settings defined in palette-vars.liquid across all surfaces.

  Dark mode: pass dark_background_color/dark_text_color/dark_border_color to also emit a
  second, dark-scoped block (html[data-color-mode='dark'] .color-custom-{{ section_id }}),
  computed the same way against settings.dark_page_text_color. Only worth passing for the
  handful of fixed-id "UI chrome" surfaces (popover/drawer/badges, see
  snippets/theme-styles-variables.liquid) that are meant to flip with the toggle — arbitrary
  per-section/per-block custom background colors intentionally keep their authored color in
  both modes, so don't pass dark_* for those.

  @param {string} [background_color] - Custom background color. Nothing is output when blank or fully transparent (alpha == 0).
  @param {string} [text_color] - Explicit text color. Skips smart contrast when provided.
  @param {string} [border_color] - Optional border color to override if contrast is insufficient.
  @param {string} section_id - Unique identifier for scoping the CSS variables.
  @param {boolean} [skip_contrast] - When true, apply only the background color without any contrast overrides.
  @param {string} [preset] - One of 'content' (default) or 'ui'. Controls which token categories are emitted.
  @param {string} [dark_background_color] - Dark-mode counterpart of background_color. Presence (non-blank) is what triggers the dark pass.
  @param {string} [dark_text_color] - Dark-mode counterpart of text_color.
  @param {string} [dark_border_color] - Dark-mode counterpart of border_color.

  @example
  {% render 'contrast-override',
    background_color: block.settings.background_color,
    text_color: block.settings.text_color,
    border_color: block.settings.border_color,
    section_id: section_id
  %}
  @example
  {% render 'contrast-override',
    background_color: settings.popover_background_color,
    text_color: settings.popover_text_color,
    border_color: settings.popover_border_color,
    dark_background_color: settings.dark_popover_background_color,
    dark_text_color: settings.dark_popover_text_color,
    dark_border_color: settings.dark_popover_border_color,
    section_id: 'popover',
    preset: 'ui'
  %}
{% enddoc %}

{% render 'contrast-vars',
  background_color: background_color,
  text_color: text_color,
  border_color: border_color,
  section_id: section_id,
  skip_contrast: skip_contrast,
  preset: preset,
  page_text_color: settings.page_text_color,
  selector_scope: ''
%}

{% if settings.enable_dark_mode and dark_background_color != blank %}
  {% render 'contrast-vars',
    background_color: dark_background_color,
    text_color: dark_text_color,
    border_color: dark_border_color,
    section_id: section_id,
    skip_contrast: skip_contrast,
    preset: preset,
    page_text_color: settings.dark_page_text_color,
    selector_scope: "html[data-color-mode='dark'] "
  %}
{% endif %}
